# GrowFlow — Phase 01: Complete Frontend Page & Screen Inventory

**Project:** GrowFlow  
**Phase:** 01 — Complete Frontend Page & Screen Inventory  
**Status:** 🟡 DRAFT — AWAITING REVIEW

## 1. Phase Objective

Phase 01 establishes the complete user-facing frontend surface of GrowFlow before frontend architecture, visual design, and page-by-page implementation.

It answers:

> **What is the complete frontend surface of GrowFlow?**

This inventory is intentionally exhaustive. It documents meaningful pages, screens, workspaces, workflows, contextual views, global interactions, and system states. Exact routes and visual implementation are deferred to later phases.

## 2. Frontend Surface Model

A “page” means a meaningful user-facing frontend surface and does not necessarily mean one unique URL.

A surface may eventually be implemented as:

```text
PAGE
 ├── Sub-page / Detail
 ├── Workspace View
 ├── Workflow Screen
 ├── Tabbed View
 ├── Drawer / Modal
 └── System State
```

This allows complete documentation without unnecessary route fragmentation.

